  "2026-09-27T12:26:27.673Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: GH-1326 and all-status Windows nightly searches found historical closed failures including pm-gh1075 and pm-ul9rye; this exact run and bundled init timeout have no owner. Run 36310799887 log establishes a distinct shard-1 failure."
  "2026-09-27T23:32:23.508Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked real bundled init suite 36/36 passed; the all-package install assertion remains intact with a 90-second test budget. Packed npm, npx, bunx, package catalog, calendar, and SDK consumer smoke passed. Full coverage passed 9380 tests at 100/100/100/100. Required Windows Node 24 PR check remains pending."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:41:21.377Z","harness:codex",Hosted Nightly Validation run 36310799887 retried bundled all-package init and timed out at exactly the old 30-second test limit on Windows. The test still performs the full real package install and assertions with an explicit 90-second budget.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:41:23.077Z","harness:codex",A wall-clock test limit must account for the slowest hosted platform when the behavior under test is real bundled package installation; preserve the assertion rather than stubbing the install.
